    "title": "NKY Special Olympians shine bright - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Marc Hardin ,\n13 hours ago When Team Kentucky marched into the 2026 Special Olympics USA Games in Minneapolis, four athletes from northern Kentucky carried not just their team colors, but the pride of their hometowns. Over six days of competition late last month, Maddie Brinkman of Union, Carmen Widener of Burlington, Daniel Hewitt of Erlanger, and Chris Revay of Fort Mitchell delivered performances that were as accomplished as they were admired. Read full article",
